---
components: ["ArcDiagram"]
description: Arc diagram lays nodes along one line and draws each link as an arc, for adjacency and sequence such as imports, citations, or co-occurrence.
---

<script>
  import { ArcDiagram } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";

  const modules = [
    { id: "app", bundle: "core" },
    { id: "router", bundle: "core" },
    { id: "store", bundle: "core" },
    { id: "button", bundle: "ui" },
    { id: "dialog", bundle: "ui" },
    { id: "table", bundle: "ui" },
    { id: "http", bundle: "data" },
    { id: "cache", bundle: "data" },
    { id: "auth", bundle: "data" },
  ];
  const imports = [
    ["app", "router", 4], ["app", "store", 6], ["app", "button", 2], ["app", "dialog", 1],
    ["router", "store", 3], ["dialog", "button", 5], ["table", "button", 2], ["table", "store", 3],
    ["store", "http", 8], ["store", "cache", 4], ["http", "auth", 3], ["auth", "cache", 1],
    ["cache", "store", 2],
  ].map(([from, to, n]) => ({ from, to, n }));

  const chapters = Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) => ({ id: `Ch ${i + 1}` }));
  const references = [
    [1, 3], [1, 7], [2, 3], [3, 5], [3, 9], [4, 5], [5, 6], [5, 11], [6, 8], [7, 8], [8, 12], [9, 10], [10, 12], [2, 11],
  ].map(([from, to]) => ({ from: `Ch ${from}`, to: `Ch ${to}` }));

  let selected = null;
</script>

`ArcDiagram` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`. With a single-theme stylesheet such as `g100.css`, load the matching `viz-g100.css` instead. The subpackage is experimental: its API may change in a minor release.

It is the one-dimensional network: every node on one line, in an order that means something, and a semicircle per link. It suits adjacency and sequence, where the order carries information a force layout would throw away. A [ChordDiagram](/components/ChordDiagram) suits flows with amounts between every pair, and a [LayeredGraph](/components/LayeredGraph) a dependency graph with ranks.

## Basic

Pass `nodes` with an `id` and `links` read with `source` and `target`. Nodes sit in the order given; set `value` on a link to scale its stroke.

<ArcDiagram nodes={chapters} links={references} id="id" source="from" target="to" title="Chapter cross-references" labelSpace={48} />

## Group and order

Set `group` to color the nodes, and the links leaving them, by a field with a legend. Set `sort` to `"group"` to gather the groups, or `"degree"` to put the most linked first. Set `directed` to arc a link that runs backward under the line.

<ArcDiagram nodes={modules} links={imports} id="id" group="bundle" source="from" target="to" value="n" sort="group" directed title="Module imports, by bundle" />

## Selection

Bind `selected` or listen for `select`, whose detail carries the node and every link touching it. Hover or focus a node to fade the links that do not touch it.

<ArcDiagram nodes={modules} links={imports} id="id" group="bundle" source="from" target="to" value="n" sort="degree" bind:selected title="Pick a module" />

## Accessibility

The chart is a single tab stop. Right and Left walk the nodes along the line, announcing each with its group and how many links touch it; those links light up. Enter or Space selects, Escape clears. The figure also holds a visually hidden list of every node and every link.
